  know:'You need the tray, dough balls and the spacing lesson — "give each cookie room for its neighbour." The rule, said at every bake: "the tray is hot; we wait; grown-ups lift."',
  why:'Tray burns are a classic little-kitchen injury, and they are preventable with one rehearsed sentence. Meanwhile the arranging job keeps small hands fully in the baking.',
