  know:'You need the machine and the brew ritual, watched from outside: water in, filter in, button on — "drip, drip, drip." The rule: "the jug is hot; grown-ups pour." The counter-offer: your child pours the COLD drinks.',
  why:'A child with a real pouring job (juice! water!) stays in the serving business safely, while the hot rule lands where it belongs — on the machine that is genuinely hot.',
