  vocab:'coffee maker, drip, filter, jug, hot, pour',
  teach:'1) Name the machine: "coffee maker! The morning machine."\n2) Watch a brew from the outside: "water in the top… coffee in the filter… button — drip, drip, drip!"\n3) The rule while it drips: "the jug gets HOT. The coffee maker is a grown-up machine — we watch."\n4) The counter-offer at the fridge: "YOUR pouring job — the cold drinks! Juice for the table… water for the cups."\n5) Pour and serve. Two pouring jobs, two temperatures, one safe system.',
  say:'"Coffee maker! Drip, drip, drip — the morning machine. Water in, coffee in… the jug fills up. The jug is HOT — grown-ups only. And YOUR job: the cold drinks! Juice for everyone — pour with two hands!"',
