  real:'Coffee machines hum in every kitchen and hotel. Each brew is a free rehearsal: "dripping… the jug is hot… my job is the juice." Roles confirmed, everywhere.',
  play:'Family Café: the cold-drink station is the child\u2019s — jug of juice, cups, two-hand pouring, orders taken. The coffee maker hums in the background, officially out of bounds and therefore uninteresting.',
  safety:'The jug and the plate under it stay hot for hours — long after the drip stops. Rule: the coffee maker is a grown-up machine, watched and named; the child owns the cold-drink pouring.',
